MK wrote:
> 
> On Wed, 16 Dec 1998 16:41:58 +0100, Nguyen-Dai Quy
> <DaiQuy.nguyen@ulg.ac.be> wrote:
> 
> >Hi,
> >Howto download a file via ftp (anonymous) automatically by using
> >crontab ?
> >I try in my cron file:
> >0 2 25 12 * /home/users/quy/mydownload
> >
> >With my script "mydownload". Which command I can put in my script
> >for automatic downloading ?
> 
> man wget
> man lftp
> man pavuk
> 
> and lots of other packages
> 

ftp can be used to do it.

First create a file ~/.netrc contains a line like this:
default anonymous guest@

Then create a command file ftp_commands like this:
open ftp_site_address
cd /dir/to/the/file
lcd /local/dir/to/put/the/file
bin (or asc)
get name_of_the_file
bye

Now, issue the command:
ftp < ftp_commands

To do it via crontab, just put last command in "mydownload".



