edward k scheer wrote:
> 
> After rebooting Digital UNIX 4.0 (after it had run just fine for 6
> mothns), I can' t get into single user mode. After beginning
> the boot process, an endless stream of  this message:
> "kloadsrv: kernal load server already running"
> appears.
> Did my disk get corrupted. Any ides

The process of booting is rather simple:

1. bootstrap
2. load kernel (/vmunix)
3. spawn process "init %flag", flag is what you pass from SRM console,
-s or -a
4. "init" reads /etc/inittab and launches appropriate processes.

Your inittab should look like:

is:3:initdefault:
ss:Ss:wait:/sbin/rc0 shutdown < /dev/console > /dev/console 2>&1
s0:0:wait:/sbin/rc0 off < /dev/console > /dev/console 2>&1
fs:23:wait:/sbin/bcheckrc < /dev/console > /dev/console 2>&1
kls:Ss:sysinit:/sbin/kloadsrv < /dev/console > /dev/console 2>&1
sysconfig:23:wait:/sbin/init.d/autosysconfig start < /dev/console >
/dev/console 2>&1
update:23:wait:/sbin/update > /dev/console 2>&1
it:23:wait:/sbin/it < /dev/console > /dev/console 2>&1
kmk:3:wait:/sbin/kmknod > /dev/console 2>&1
s2:23:wait:/sbin/rc2 < /dev/console > /dev/console 2>&1
s3:3:wait:/sbin/rc3 < /dev/console > /dev/console 2>&1
cons:1234:respawn:/usr/sbin/getty console console vt100

The line:

kls:Ss:sysinit:/sbin/kloadsrv < /dev/console > /dev/console 2>&1

is what loads "Kernel Loadable Module server". Now, either your
/etc/inittab got corrupted or your kloadsrv. Try booting from CD with
Digital UNIX. (If that fails, suspect hardware) Mount and inspect your
root FS. Try checking it with "fsck" for UFS, or "verify" for AdvFS.

Nix.
-- 
