You don't say what version of DU you are running, but I built 5.50
on a DU 40.D system using DEC C as follows:
Rename the jpeg, libpng, and zlib directories to "jpeg", "libpng" and
"zlib". (No versions.)

Edit unixansi.mak. Change CFLAGS to "CFLAGS=-fast -std". (The '-std' is 
the key.)

make -f unixansi.mak

Lots of warnings, especially about hipot arguments, but no errors.

Whenever you build freeware on DU, unless there are specific DU
instructions, always specify "-std"!

If you are running DU older than 4.0, you may be stuck as the old
compiler was was ANSI.
