Brandon,

If you want to label the disk, simply use the following disklabel command:

# disklabel -r -w rz2 UNKNOWN

substituting the appropriate special disk device file for "rz2". If the
disk type is unknown, using a value of "UNKNOWN" will cause the disklabel
command to query the disk driver for the disk's geometry.

A "disklabel -r" command will then display the newly written label.

