Nikola Milutinovic <Nikola.Milutinovic@ev.co.yu> wrote:
: Arago wrote:
: > I would know how increase the resolution of CDE desktop. (now is 640*480).
: > I would like have it displayed at 800*600.

: Strictly speaking, screen resolution has nothing to do with CDE. CDE is
: a "X Windows environment". 
: <snip>
: So, you need to change the resolution of X Windows. The file containing
: the configuration is: /usr/lib/X11/Xserver.conf
:
: I'm not sure what the actual arguments are, but I'm sure I've seen it.

The file to modify is actually:

   /usr/lib/X11/xdm/Xservers

Change the following line:

   :0 local /usr/bin/X11/X

to the following:

   :0 local /usr/bin/X11/X -screen0 800

and either reboot or simply stop and restart X by issuing the following
command:

   # /sbin/rc3.d/S95xlogin restart   (assuming Digital UNIX v4.0x)

