: 	I just bought an Alpha Station 200 from a reseller without a video
: card.  I've been having an incredibly difficult time getting the system to
: work; I bought a PCI 2.1 compatible video card, thinking that would be
: enough.  With the card in there, the LEDs on the back of the machine
: indicate an unspecified failure.  Without the card in there, I get an LED
: sequence indicating a successful launch of the SRM console. 
: 	Rather than asking for specific recommendations on cards which
: would work, I thought it might be better to ask if anybody has any
: suggestions about where to find additional information about which cards
: might work.  Suggestions?

Look at: http://www.workstation.digital.com/products/a200/io2.html

I believe that the "DEC864" mentioned therein is a S3 Trio64 card.  No
guarantees, though.

As far as a compatible video card, have you ever noticed that when you buy a
video card for a PC, they come with drivers?  That's because, although they
might conform to the PCI spec for proper operation within a system, they're
all programmed just a bit differently.  I suspect that the AS200 console is
kinda particular about what type of card it sees.

Make sure you visit http://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/ to make
sure you have the latest firmware for your machine.  Depending on the actual
age of the machine, you may be able to update the firmware, and maybe even get
your [unnamed] video card to work.

        Stu



