Nikola Milutinovic <Nikola.Milutinovic@ev.co.yu> wrote:
> >     Is there any other way to copy that disk in a way that it can
> > recover more info ?
> 
> A read failure is a read failure. No "miracle program" can assist you on
> that situation.

I once had a disk develop bad sectors and it was critical to recover the
data on the disk.  Turns out the read errors were intermittent, i.e. if
you kept re-trying each bad block, eventually you would manage to get good
data off it.  I wrote a little C program which just opened the raw disk
and kept trying to read each block until it didn't get an error, then
wrote that block out to some other drive.  Took a long time, but
eventually it managed to read the whole disk.

This was on an SMD drive.  Don't know enough about SCSI drives to know if
the same technique might work.

-- 
