Nguyen-Dai Quy <DaiQuy.nguyen@ulg.ac.be> writes:
|Howto download a file via ftp (anonymous) automatically by using
|crontab ?
|I try in my cron file:
|0 2 25 12 * /home/users/quy/mydownload
|
|With my script "mydownload". Which command I can put in my script
|for automatic downloading ?
|
|In the interactive mode, I have to do :
|#ftp ftp.xxxx.com
|.... anonymous
|.... myaddress..
|.... cd ....
|.... get file
|..... bye for exit
|
|Any ideas for help ?

Try using one of the following:

lynx -dump ftp://ftpserver.wherever.com/directory/file > local-file-name

wget ftp://ftpserver.wherever.com/directory/file

Both lynx and wget are free software (http://lynx.browser.org and
ftp://prep.ai.mit.edu/pub/gnu respectively).

If PORT vs. PASV mode is of concern to you (e.g. if you are behind a
firewall that lets one but not the other through), be aware that lynx
defaults to PORT and must have one of the source files changed before
compiling to make it use PASV mode (grep for NO_PORT).  wget defaults
to PORT but has a command line option to use PASV mode.

