You could try writing a perl script with the Net::FTP module and then
schedule it with cron.  This is a part of the small script we use at my
work:

use Net::FTP;
&main
sub Main  {
  $ftp = Net::FTP->new ("ftp.server.com");
  $ftp->login("anonymous","anonymous@somewhere.com");
  $ftp->binary();
  $ftp->cwd("/pub");
  $ftp->get("file.zip");
  $ftp->close();
}                     

