Rolf Gitt wrote:
> 
> Hi:
> 
> I'm using an AlphaServer 2000 running DEC Unix V3.2C. We're now having
> periodic problems where the mouse and keyboard freeze and I can't do
> anything.
> 
> I've used a telnet session to attach to the server and tried to restart the
> X-Windows/Motif GUI (using ./xdm stop followed by ./xdm start from the
> /sbin/init.d directory). This restarts the GUI interface, however the mouse
> and keyboard are still frozen.
> 
> In the past I've issued a shutdown -r now  from the telnet session to reboot
> the server, which (obviously) gets rid of the keyboard/mouse problem on
> reboot. However rebooting is not ideal! I'm wondering if there's any way to
> restart/reinitialize the mouse and keyboard drivers without rebooting the
> entire server (and without interfering with the end users).

Alas, all Alphas use PS/2 keyboard and mouse. Once detached during the
up-time, they are invalidated until next reboot. You should check for
two things. You could be suffering from statical discharges. A colleague
of mine had that problem, whenever she wore a certain suit, she would
freeze keyboard several times a day.

Secondly, there could be something wrong with the connectors.

Nix.



