: 	- unlink(2)		- remove it
: 	- symlink(2)		- create it

Well, strictly speaking this aint true on all unices (it may be true for
Sunos and/or Solaris - I just don't know). On most unices it is also
possible to lstat() a symbolic link, and on some it is possible to 
lchown() and readlink() it. Unless I am mistaken, later versions of 
Irix also have lchmod() (which, like lchown(), has no real meaning, 
but was added due to the popular demand).

(readlink(), lstat(), and lchown() are actually required by XPG4 UNIX,
so that I am sure they are also supported by Solaris, if not by SunOS).

: lrwxrwxrwx		SunOS 4/Solaris 2&7
: l---------		Irix (others?)

: Some may just use the user's umask() in creating them, (DU)?

DU creates symlinks with 0777 regardless of the users' umask. Irix
(ay least 5.* and 6.[0-4]) does indeed uses users' umask.

Regards,

/Serge.P



