gabriel_ronin@my-dejanews.com wrote:
: Does anyone know where I can find an example print filter that is not

This is an example for HP printers:

#!/bin/sh
# Filter for HP-DJ/LJ with 66 lines per page
#     Margin + condensed + LF -> CRLF
#
#\\033\E        # reset
#\\033\&l0O     # portrait = 0, 1 : landscape
#\\033\&l6D     # 6 lines per inch 
#\\033\&l70P    # formlen = 70 lines
#\\033\&l3E     # TOF = 2 lines                       
#\\033\&l66F    # max lines = 66 
#\\033\&a0E     # Left start = 0  ?
#\\033\&k2G     # LF -> CR+LF
#\\033\(s12H    # 12 char per inch   
#\\033\&a16L    # left margin in char
#\\033\&l1S     # 0=einseitig, 1=Hoch- 2=Quer-Duplex
#\\033\(0N      # unix charset
#\\033\%-12345X # ps, eps end 

echo \\033\E\\033\&l0O\\033\&l6D\\033\&l70P\\033\&l2E\\033\&l66F
echo \\033\&k2G\\033\(s12H\\033\&a12L\\033\&l0S\\033\(0N
cat -
echo \\033%-12345X 

------
Use this as if. Remember inputfilters were ignored on remote printers.

Juergen



