Remote printers ignore the lpr/print options stuffed in the control file
that is passed to the printer.

Chaining queues is one way to implement file preprocessing for remote
printing however the banner page will always display the owner as root
or daemon. I forgot which one gets printed.  If you don't use banner pages
this may be an acceptable solution.

Another method is to use a script that calls a print filter to preformat
the file then submits it to the queue. The banner page will display the
correct owner.

