I don't have an Epson printer and my Epson documentation is not complete.
However this should get you in the ball park.

The file below is for use with the pcfof print filter provided in V4.0D.

Make sure there are no spaces or tabs at the end of any line in the file. If
there are it will be printed.

----- cut here ----
! epson.pcf
!
! Installing:
!
!       Copy this file to /usr/lbin/pcf/epson.pcf
!       chmod 644 /usr/lbin/pcf/epson.pcf
!       Use lprsetup to create a printcap entry for an ln17 printer.
!       Edit the printcap entry and change +Cln17.pcf to +Cepson.pcf .
!
! Notes:
!
!       Default cpi is 12.
!       'lpr -Ocpi15 file' may select cpi of 15
!
!       Add additional Epson setup commands at 'init seq:'.
!       \033 is the octal code for ESCAPE.
!       Entering \000 is not allowed.
!
!-
format version:003
! Filter Types: PPL, PCL, ASCII, XF
filter type:ASCII
auto passthru:Y
reset:\033@
reset delay:0
! Set cpi to 12?
init seq:\033M
init delay:0
term seq:\033@
term delay:0
auto reset:N
orientation:portrait
portrait:
portrait lines:66
portrait columns:0
landscape:
landscape lines:66
landscape columns:0
landscape threshold:
wrap line:N
wrap line mark:
newline:\015\012
return:\015
newpage:\015\014
eojnewpage:
backspace:\010
tab:\011
tab width:8
tab expansion:N
! Set cpi to 15?
define cpi15:\033g





