Sandlin,William wrote:
> 
> I'm using the Korn shell under Unix 4.0 and have a number of aliases
> being defined in .profile.  The application I am working with requires
> that I perform some management functions as the root.  My problem is
> that I loose all of my aliases when I su (the documentation says this
> is supposed to happen).
> 
> How can these be preserved??  If they cannot be preserved, is there a
> profile that is executed when I su that I could also have the aliases
> defined in.

You could create a secondary root account, with a uid of zero
but with a different login, password, home directory etc. than
root.  You can then customize that account identically to yours.
When the need arises, you just "su -" to that account and change
directory back to where you were.  You could even make the account's
home directory be the normal maintenance directory for the
application (if there is such a thing).

Whatever you do, DON'T CUSTOMIZE ROOT.  root has to be able to
login in single-user mode even if the network is down, or /usr
is corrupted, etc.



