So shall we assume you are making a shell script?

In C-Shell, you could try:

	$ set DATE=`date`
	$ echo $DATE
	Wed Dec 2 08:29:09 EST 1998

In Bourne or Korn Shell:

	$ DATE=`date`
	$ echo $DATE
	Wed Dec 2 08:34:29 EST 1998

Check out the man pages on date to see how you can manipulate the
date/time output format to suit your needs. Regardless of format, the
output is in string unless otherwise conoluted.

