Joe Hargis wrote:

> I have been backing up files with the vdump command, speciffically
> "vdump -0 /" or "vdump -0 /usr", or whatever I wanted to dump.  No
> problem.
>
> The system I use was (yesterday) upgraded from dunix v4.0b to v4.0d.
> The above commands worked fine before the upgrade, and they work fine
> on other systems we have that  are running 4.0d.
>
> Now, I can dump one file system as above, but when I try to dump the
> next one, I get the error message "vdump:  device </dev/rmt0h> is
> OFFLINE".  I tried several things, but after I finally rebooted the
> system, it worked for one dump.  When I tried to do another one I got
> the same error message again.
>
> It would be nice to not have to reboot every time I want to dump a
> partition.
>
> Anyone know what I'm doing wrong and how to fix it?
>
> Thanks in advance,
> Joe

You are using the rewinding device, /dev/rmt0h. Change your vdump to use
the nonrewinding device /dev/nrmt0h. Your other option is to use the -NU
flags to vdump. This will keep it from rewinding and unloading the tape
when it is done backing up to a rewinding device.




