Are you running shutdown as root?  Only root has authority to shut down
your system.

Post the results of the following:

# ls -l `which shutdown`

or if that turns up blank:

# ls -l /sbin/shutdown /sbin/halt

These packages are part of the SysVinit RPM.  You can verify this
package by typing:

# rpm --verify SysVinit

....which will list any discrepencies between the package and what is
installed on your system.  "man rpm" for more info.


> >
> > The three-fingered salute <ctrl><alt><del> is coded to initiate system
> > shutdown in most Linux distros.
> 
> In the environment KDE, I tried this but not works ! :-(

Look at your /etc/inittab file.  It should have two lines like:

   # Trap CTRL-ALT-DELETE
   ca::ctraltdel:/sbin/shutdown -t3 -r now

If you can't find it, post the entire file.


