Remember you may also need write permission to the directory ...

Some braindead (or otherwise) software works on a temporary copy, and
when you hit "save" it deletes the original and renames the copy. That's
why you get permissions being "lost" (ie it isn't the original file) and
you also get weirdos where you think you have permission to the file...
you're not accessing the file you think you are :-(

And some properly written software is aware of this and tries both
routes to see which works :-)
